<http://data.silknow.org/object/82c761fc-8752-325a-98b9-7cff275b70d4/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "One pair of Manchu horse-hoof shoes for women of high-ranking families in coral silk satin upper embroidered with goldfishes in green, blue and beige silk thread, and edged with black silk satin.Vertical seams at toe had leather strip and loose blue silk thread stitched together inserted to hold the shape. The bottom of the shoe is most likely padded with layers of cotton to prevent jarring when walking. Its tall wooden heel has a slightly curved 'horse-hoof' ('mati'??) shape with hemp-covered sole."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/82c761fc-8752-325a-98b9-7cff275b70d4> .

